    12	# - NAME is per run (ts-f2a, ts-f2b), not per launch tag (review r1): one launch lock, balance baseline and spend record
    13	#   per run, so two launches of a run never overlap and a launch is refused while the previous one's spend is unrecorded.
    14	#   The launch tag names this launch's reservation (<run tag>-<tag>, category followup); any other open reservation of
    15	#   the run (an unrecorded earlier launch) refuses the launch. One validated ledger snapshot gives PRIOR and is pushed.
    16	# - PRIOR is not an operator input: it is the spend the ledger records for this run's tag (the same rule as the drivers'
    17	#   guards.ledger_spend), and a reservation for the run tag must cover the watchdog bound HARD x CAP - PRIOR.
    18	# - Before every paid step on the pod (the reproduction gate included) the remote script checks the STOP file and the soft
    19	#   deadline, then runs guards.py admit with the plan's cap, the ceiling MAXCPH, the live pod's request time, this
    20	#   launch's attempts file and the ledger (both pushed to the pod before the remote script starts; neither can change
    21	#   while the pod runs), the run tag and the step's estimate; the step starts only on exit 0.
